{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Avram said: Adonai.</b> With alef-dalet. <b>What will You give me, and I go childless.</b> Alone, without an heir. Even though it had already been said to him, 'To your seed I will give this land,' at first, he thought that through prayer he would merit children; and when he saw that he delayed in begetting, it occurred to him that perhaps sin had caused it — therefore he said, <b>and I go childless.</b>" "<b>He is Damesek Eliezer.</b> He was the grandson of Nimrod the wicked."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:16.905840376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}